<node id="11104642" title="Re^2: The error says the value is uninitialized, but it works anyway" created="2019-08-18 03:42:51" updated="2019-08-18 03:42:51" _doctext_mode="strict"><type id="11">note</type>
<author id="830549">haukex</author>
<doctext field_name="doctext">&lt;blockquote&gt;&lt;i&gt;&lt;c&gt;undef ne $string&lt;/c&gt; if &lt;c&gt;$string&lt;/c&gt; is a defined value.&lt;/i&gt;&lt;/blockquote&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Sorry, but no: &lt;c&gt;$string = ""&lt;/c&gt; is a [doc://defined] value, and &lt;c&gt;undef eq ""&lt;/c&gt;. What's happening is that &lt;c&gt;eq&lt;/c&gt; forces string context on its arguments and &lt;c&gt;undef&lt;/c&gt; is converted to &lt;c&gt;""&lt;/c&gt;, with a warning, which of course is the same thing as the string &lt;c&gt;""&lt;/c&gt;. &lt;c&gt;eq&lt;/c&gt; is not a test for [doc://defined]ness, only [doc://defined] does that - &lt;c&gt;undef eq undef&lt;/c&gt; not because they are both &lt;c&gt;undef&lt;/c&gt;, but because &lt;c&gt;"" eq ""&lt;/c&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
</doctext>
